Without rpi-image-gen, you'd need to:

Manually run debootstrap to create root filesystem
Configure bootloader and firmware
Set up partitions and filesystems
Write custom scripts for everything
Handle Raspberry Pi hardware quirks yourself

rpi-image-gen automates all of that and provides a clean, maintainable way to define and build custom Raspberry Pi images using Debian packages.

