✅ GitHub hook trigger for GITScm polling - CHECK THIS ⭐
Why: This is the "proper" way to trigger builds automatically when you push to GitHub.
How it works:

You push code to GitHub
GitHub sends webhook to Jenkins
Jenkins automatically starts build

⚠️ IMPORTANT: This only works if:

Jenkins is publicly accessible (has public IP/domain)
OR you're using a tunneling service (ngrok, localhost.run)
OR Jenkins is on a cloud instance

If Jenkins is on your laptop behind a router, webhooks WON'T work (GitHub can't reach your laptop).

⚪ Poll SCM - CHECK THIS as backup/alternative
Why: If webhooks don't work (Jenkins on laptop), polling is the fallback.
Schedule: H/5 **** (checks GitHub every 5 minutes)
How it works:

Jenkins asks GitHub every 5 minutes: "Any new commits?"
If yes → starts build
Less efficient than webhooks, but works everywhere

