Solution 2: Use Docker Agent ⭐ Recommended
Jenkins runs on Windows, but builds happen inside Linux Docker containers.

//--------------------//
//--------------------//
//--------------------//

Jenkins workspace is on Windows: C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\workspace\CoinOS-Build\
Jenkins converts to forward slashes: C:/ProgramData/Jenkins/.jenkins/workspace/CoinOS-Build/
Docker needs Linux path: Expects something like /workspace or /mnt/c/...
Path translation fails: Docker can't map Windows C:/ to Linux filesystem


//--------------------//
//--------------------//
//--------------------//


1. Jenkins Controller (Windows) checks out code
   ↓
   Clones to: C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\workspace\CoinOS-Build\
   ↓
2. Jenkins reads the Jenkinsfile from that checkout
   ↓
3. Jenkins sees: agent { docker { ... } }
   ↓
4. Jenkins tries to start Docker container
   ↓
5. Jenkins tries to MOUNT the Windows workspace into container
   ↓
6. ❌ FAILS - Can't mount C:/ path into Linux container


reuseNode true means: "Use the SAME workspace that was checked out on Windows"
Jenkins tries to mount C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\... into the Docker container
Docker says: "I can't work with Windows paths!"


